The graph shows the value of a mixing plant depreciated by the straight-line method.

[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[width=9cm,height=7cm,axis lines=left,axis line style={-{Stealth}},xmin=0,xmax=8.6,ymin=0,ymax=22000,xtick={0,1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8},ytick={0,2500,5000,7500,10000,12500,15000,17500,20000},grid=both,samples=2,clip=false,scaled ticks=false,ticklabel style={font=\scriptsize,/pgf/number format/fixed},xlabel={Years, $n$},ylabel={Value (\$)},ylabel near ticks]
\addplot[thick,blue,domain=0:8]{20000 - 2500*x};
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]

Use the graph to find the annual depreciation amount and the value of the plant after $6$ years.
